t your changes have the desired effects e.g. run unit tests, make sure code builds, etc. before claiming that the task is complete.\n- After you've completed your task and verified that \n<truncated 320 bytes>\n for feedback and approval.\nAfter reading the document, the user should understand the key technical details of your plan, and be able to make an informed decision on whether to approve it.\nThis document should be very detailed, including code snippets, diffs, mermaid diagrams, verification strategies, and background information.\n\n**Format**: Use the following format, omitting any irrelevant sections:\n\n## [Goal Description]\nProvide a brief description of the problem, any background context, and what the change accomplishes.\n\n## User Review Required\nDocument anything that requires user review or feedback, for example, breaking changes or significant design decisions. Use GitHub alerts (IMPORTANT/WARNING/CAUTION) to highlight critical items.\n\n## Open Questions\nAny clarifying or design questions for the user that will impact the implementation plan. Use GitHub alerts (IMPORTANT/WARNING/CAUTION) to highlight critical items.\n\n## Proposed Changes\nGroup files by component (e.g., package, feature area, dependency layer) and order logically (dependencies first). Separate components with horizontal rules for visual clarity.\n\n### [Component Name]\nSummary of what will change in this component with explicit code snippets and diffs. For specific files, Use [NEW] and [DELETE] to demarcate new and deleted files, for example:\n#### [MODIFY] file basename\n#### [NEW] file basename\n#### [DELETE] file basename\n\n## Verification Plan\nSummary of how you will verify that your changes have the desired effects.\n\n### Automated Tests\nExact commands to run automated tests\n\n### Manual Verification\nInstructions for what the user should manually verify.\n\n# Walkthrough\nPath: <Artifact Directory>/walkthrough.md\n\n**Purpose**: After completing work, summarize what you accomplished. Update an existing walkthrough for related follow-up work rather than creating a new one.\n\n**Document**:\n- Changes made\n- What was tested\n- Validation results\n\nEmbed screenshots and recordings to visually demonstrate UI changes and user flows.</PLAN>\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":212,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T18:15:01Z","input_tokens":3987,"cache_read_tokens":77940,"output_tokens":2180,"thinking":"**Assessing the Plan**\n\nI'm currently dissecting the `/plan` command, focusing on the input concerning OCR adjustments and aesthetic modifications. The user reports positive OCR progress (\"todo bien\") but highlights the need for aesthetic changes and a default template. I'm prioritizing understanding the specifics of these visual and template-related requirements.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Timeouts**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the timeout warnings and their implications for the capture process. The user encountered the predicted delays related to the Pokedex blocking text, causing delays in the `_check_capture_result` and `_wait_for_menu` steps. These timeouts confirm the need for the adjustments discussed previously. The user wants to resolve these timeouts.\n\n\n**Implementing the Plan**\n\nI've outlined concrete actions: resolving the Ditto delay and the escape bug. I'll maintain the current default template, avoiding GUI file modifications as requested. Finally, I'll prepare a Git push with clear commit messages.\n\n\n**Refining the Approach**\n\nI'm now focusing on a new plan to resolve the Ditto delay. I've broken down the problem: the Pokédex blocks the screen, causing unnecessary timeouts. My solution involves adjusting the code to assume victory and quickly skip the delay. I'm also preparing for the Git integration, including the `add`, `commit`, and `push` commands. The user clarified they want me to fix the issue. I'll update the plan and seek quick approval before executing.\n\n\n**Updating the Code**\n\nI've made crucial code modifications to `src/modes/base.py`. In `_check_capture_result()`, I'm now assuming a successful capture after the timeout. I've also added steps to clean up in `_capture_sequence()` by mashing 'X' to close the Pokédex. I've tweaked the `run_away()` function for added reliability. Finally, I'm working to refine the timeout in the `_wait_for_map()` function in `single.py`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"Append":"false","ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Plan paso a paso (ADHD friendly) para arreglar los timeouts, el escape y guardar en Git.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"## 🎯 El Objetivo (Resumen Rápido)\\nEse error que me pasaste es exactamente lo que te decía. Como la pantalla del Pokémon atrapado tapa todo, el bot se queda ciego.\\n1. Busca la palabra \\\"Atrapado\\\" por 12 segundos y tira el primer warning (`timed out after 60 polls`).\\n2. Luego espera el menú de batalla por 30 segundos y tira el segundo warning (`CAPTURE ENDED... 4 turns timeout/stop`).\\n\\nVamos a arreglar esto, respetar tu estética visual intacta, y respaldar todo en Git.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🛠️ Los Cambios (Paso a Paso)\\n\\n### 1. Arreglar el Delay Infinito (`src/modes/base.py`)\\nSi el bot lanza la bola y el menú no vuelve en 12 segundos, le diremos: *\\\"¡Significa que lo atrapamos, deja de esperar y cierra la ventana!\\\"*.\\n* **Cambio:** Retornaremos `True` (Éxito) en lugar de `False` al terminar los 60 intentos.\\n* **Limpieza:** Haremos que el bot presione la tecla 'X' 5 veces seguidas rápido al terminar la captura para cerrar la Pokédex.\\n\\n### 2. Arreglar el Escape Fallido (`src/controller.py` y `src/modes/single.py`)\\nPara que no empiece a caminar chocando la pared mientras sigue en batalla:\\n* **Cambio 1:** Le daremos un respiro de `0.1s` a las teclas direccionales al elegir \\\"Huir\\\" (Run) para que el juego no se las trague por el lag.\\n* **Cambio 2:** Si el bot intenta huir y después de 4 segundos la batalla sigue ahí, **presionará huir de nuevo** automáticamente.\\n\\n### 3. Estética y UI (MANDATO DE RESPETO)\\n* **NO** tocaré tu archivo `main_gui.py` ni ninguna plantilla XML/JSON de interfaz. Todo lo visual se queda tal cual lo tienes ahora como default.\\n\\n### 4. Git y Respaldo\\nCuando el código esté inyectado y funcionando, ejecutaré en la terminal:\\n1. `git add .`\\n2. `git commit -m \\\"Fix: Solucionado delay post-captura de Ditto, blindaje de huida y preservación estética\\\"`\\n3. `git push` (Si tienes configurado el remoto).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🚦 User Review Required\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> **Aprobación Final**\\n> Al ser auDHD, quiero mantener esto súper directo y sin sobrecargas para ti. \\n>\n<truncated 188 bytes>","Description":"\"Plan estructurado y claro para arreglar bugs de visión/teclado y hacer push a Git.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Brian\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity-cli\\\\brain\\\\dab6a3d4-72ff-45ea-898a-cdc9ce4a7ca1\\\\plan_fix_ditto_delay.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing ADHD-friendly plan\"","toolSummary":"\"Plan update\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
